BT /F2 11 Tf 50.0 636.0 Td (1. Memory, Pointers & Array Viva Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 619.0 Td (- Q1: What is the difference between malloc\(\) and calloc\(\)?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 603.0 Td (  A: malloc\(\) allocates uninitialized memory; calloc\(\) allocates contiguous memory and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 589.0 Td (  zeroes all bits.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 573.0 Td (- Q2: Explain the difference between array name 'a' and '&a' in C.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 557.0 Td (  A: 'a' decays to a pointer to first element \(int*\); '&a' is a pointer to the entire) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 543.0 Td (  array \(int\(*\)[N]\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50.0 519.0 Td (2. Functions & Structures Viva Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 502.0 Td (- Q3: What is the difference between Structure and Union in C?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 486.0 Td (  A: Structure allocates memory equal to sum of all members; Union shares memory equal) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 472.0 Td (  to largest member.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 456.0 Td (- Q4: What is a Dangling Pointer and how can it be prevented?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 440.0 Td (  A: A pointer pointing to deallocated memory; prevent by assigning ptr = NULL) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 426.0 Td (  immediately after free\(ptr\).) Tj ET
